Module Interface Overview

A. Top Action Controls (Left to Right):
1.	Import Network: Load your EPANET .INP file
2.	Set Scenario and Run: Configure water quality simulations
3.	Explore Paths: Find and analyze flow routes
4.	Graphical Analysis: Generate charts and statistics
5.	User Guide: Access this documentation
B. Left Control Panel:
•	Display toggles: Show/hide nodes and pipes
•	Label options: Show names or values with adjustable decimal places
•	Parameter selection: Choose Water Age, Trace, or Chemical analysis
•	Size controls: Adjust visual element sizes
C. Main Network Display:
Interactive visualization showing:
•	Nodes: Circles (blue=junctions, green=tanks, red=reservoirs)
•	Pipes: Gray connecting lines
•	Current values: Water quality parameters at selected time
•	Filter highlights: Yellow elements matching your criteria
D. Right Information Panel:
•	Simulation status: Which analyses have been completed
•	Legend: Color coding reference
•	Current statistics: Data about selected elements
