Core Workflows
Workflow 1: Contamination Source Tracking
Scenario: A contaminant enters at a known location. You need to track its spread.
Steps:
1.	Load your network (Import Network button)
2.	Configure contamination scenario (Set Scenario and Run):
o	Select "Chemical Concentration" analysis
o	Set entry node (contamination source)
o	Configure concentration strength and duration
o	Click "Run Analysis"
3.	Track the spread:
o	Use the time slider to see contamination progression
o	Filter for concentration values (> threshold) to highlight affected areas
o	Enable animation to visualize movement
4.	Export findings for emergency response planning
Workflow 2: Water Age Analysis for Stagnation Zones
Scenario: Identify areas where water stays too long in the system.
Steps:
1.	Run water age analysis (Set Scenario and Run)
2.	Apply filters to focus on problematic areas:
o	Set filter to "> 48" (older than 48 hours)
o	Check "Color The Filtered" to highlight yellow
3.	Investigate specific paths (Explore Paths):
o	Select source reservoir as START point
o	Select problematic area as END point
o	Analyze all possible routes
4.	Generate reports with graphical analysis
Workflow 3: Tracer Study for Source Identification
Scenario: Determine which source serves specific customers.
Steps:
1.	Run tracer analysis from potential sources
2.	Use Explore Paths to find connection routes
3.	Compare tracer percentages along different paths
4.	Map visualization to see geographic routes
5.	Tabular analysis to get precise percentages
