Best Practices for Effective Analysis
1. Preparation Phase:
•	Ensure network has geographic coordinates for map analysis
•	Run baseline water age analysis for reference
•	Establish normal operating conditions
2. Investigation Phase:
•	Start with broad filters, then refine
•	Use multiple analysis types (water age, trace, chemical)
•	Compare different time periods
•	Document analysis parameters for reproducibility
3. Reporting Phase:
•	Use map visualizations for geographic context
•	Include tabular data for precise values
•	Document assumptions and limitations
•	Highlight critical findings clearly
4. Validation:
•	Compare with field measurements when available
•	Check for data consistency across analyses
•	Validate against known system behavior
