Tips for Efficient Use
1.	For large networks:
o	Hide labels during navigation for better performance
o	Use filters to focus on specific areas
o	Export data and analyze in smaller segments
2.	For time-based analysis:
o	Use animation for overview
o	Export time-series data for detailed statistical analysis
o	Compare specific time points rather than entire periods
3.	For reporting:
•	Capture map screenshots with annotations
•	Export tabular data for inclusion in reports
•	Document analysis parameters for reproducibility
________________________________________
Limitations and Considerations
Data Requirements:
•	Geographic coordinates needed for map visualization
•	Simulation results required for water quality analysis, so if simulation fails, the analysis will not work
•	Complete network connectivity for accurate path finding
Analysis Limitations:
•	Results based on simulation models, not field measurements
•	Assumes steady-state conditions within time steps
•	Dependent on input data quality and completeness
Practical Considerations:
•	Large networks may have performance impacts
•	Complex analyses may require multiple steps
•	Results should be validated against field data when possible

